Z||000000||kinboyatuwo||11-28-2000||02:00 PM||||Okay, have had lots of problems lately and this is the latest, it is a 2.5, '87<P>I changed the air filter and figured, what the heck, and checked the plugs while i was fiddling.<P>I have copious (want to sound edumicated) amounts of oil on my plugs.  Pulled them out and they were practically dripping.  I am looking for suggestions.  I have the same problems as Knightryder31 in the mornings and it has been running poor<BR>the exaust has a weird smell (not sure but cant compare it to food or anything i know) and has water droplets in it (it is light grey.  There is a light misty smoke in the enging when i open the oil fill cap.  <BR>does not seem to be burning oil, think it is leaking (takes about 1L every 1000 km) becaues ther are drops sometimes.<P>I have a rocker cover gasket to replace anyway, that is where i think the oil is coming from<P>i know there is a lot here but thanks to all that can help<P>Decision is coming soon, buy a new GT, upgrade the motor and fix the car, fix the problems or start one big ass bon fire<P>thanks<BR>chris<BR> <P>------------------<BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."||||reg||9
Z||000001||deceler8||11-28-2000||04:50 PM||||Your engine's probably on its last legs.<P>But before you start the bonfire, check your PCV valve and breather. If the PCV quits, the blowby gets routed into the air cleaner and burned, which can foul plugs. You'll also have lots of oil in your air cleaner.<P>Your valve stem seals are probably bad, maybe really bad. Could be that the drainback holes in your head are plugged and more oil than usual is going down the guides.<P>Just trying to be positive.<P>Maybe it's Marvel Mystery Oil time (LOL).||||reg||1
